    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5e75efd2_d7a25b5b",
        "filename": "audio/aidl/default/Module.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 548,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042638
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-09T17:14:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In my view, this case is applied when the initial configuration does not specify profiles for either type of ports. This requires the HAL module implementation-specific code to query the capabilities of the connected devices and provide them to this common part. Otherwise, the set of connected device and mix ports will be unusable, as there will be no singe configuration to suggest to the client.",
      "parentUuid": "d987c059_64256e8a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 548,
        "startChar": 61,
        "endLine": 548,
        "endChar": 83
      },
      "revId": "03ce968bf744b711f8121f1a346183b69bc10df6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e58b1383_24a36c77",
        "filename": "audio/aidl/default/Module.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 548,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003259
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-10T09:27:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes but the condition is still that at least one mix port is dynamic. It is possible that non dynamic mix ports also have a route to a device with empty profiles. This is typically the case for USB devices where the primary output or deep buffer output can be routed to USB and only the hifi output has a dynamic profile and can be routed to USB.",
      "parentUuid": "5e75efd2_d7a25b5b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 548,
        "startChar": 61,
        "endLine": 548,
        "endChar": 83
      },
      "revId": "03ce968bf744b711f8121f1a346183b69bc10df6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
